WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.088
This is an implementation guide.

2
00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:07.215
The Federal Modernization Workbook's Book
07 decided that the program's certificate

3
00:00:07.215 --> 00:00:10.465
lifecycle platform is
CyberArk Certificate Manager,

4
00:00:10.465 --> 00:00:14.149
from the vendor the agency
already uses for machine identity.

5
00:00:14.149 --> 00:00:17.366
This guide shows how to
build it, self-hosted,

6
00:00:17.366 --> 00:00:20.850
and connect it to Book 07's
design, phase by phase.

7
00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:24.062
It runs in four parts
after a short orientation.

8
00:00:24.062 --> 00:00:27.188
Part 1 builds the platform: architecture,

9
00:00:27.188 --> 00:00:31.325
the FIPS posture, console
sign-in, hardening, and backup.

10
00:00:31.325 --> 00:00:35.804
Part 2 connects the issuers: Active
Directory Certificate Services,

11
00:00:35.804 --> 00:00:39.575
the public certificate authorities,
the cloud, and Intune.

12
00:00:39.575 --> 00:00:44.013
Part 3 covers discovery, ownership
and enrollment automation.

13
00:00:44.013 --> 00:00:50.063
And Part 4 maps the build onto Book 07's
six migration waves and covers running it.

14
00:00:50.063 --> 00:00:51.374
Three ground rules.

15
00:00:51.374 --> 00:00:56.895
Every fact comes from a primary source
opened on October twenty-second,

16
00:00:56.895 --> 00:01:00.825
2026, mostly CyberArk's
version 26.1 documentation.

17
00:01:00.825 --> 00:01:03.738
Recommendations are
labeled design guidance.

18
00:01:03.738 --> 00:01:08.382
And in three places the research
corrects Book 07; I'll state the

19
00:01:08.382 --> 00:01:13.562
corrected fact each time, and Book 07
has been updated to match to match.

20
00:01:13.562 --> 00:01:19.736
Sources: Research brief,
Implementing Book 07's certificate

21
00:01:19.736 --> 00:01:26.898
lifecycle on CyberArk Certificate
Manager, Self-Hosted (verified Oct.

